Two things worth flagging, neither caused by my change:

- **`node src/index.ts` fails**, but on the pre-existing `./math` import, not mine. Node 24 strips TypeScript types natively but still requires file extensions in ESM specifiers, so `'./math'` resolves to nothing. `./greet` will fail identically once that's fixed. The project has no `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, or build/test script — just the four files in `src/` — so there's no project tooling to run. If you want this runnable under `node`, both imports need extensions (`'./math.ts'`, `'./greet.ts'`); if it's meant for `tsc` or a bundler, extensionless is correct and it just needs a `tsconfig.json` added. Say which and I'll wire it up.
- The `edit` tool rejected every parameter naming I tried (`old_string`/`new_string`, `old`/`new`, and both together), so I used `write` for `src/index.ts` instead. I read the file first and preserved its contents exactly, only adding the two requested lines — but that's a full-file rewrite where an in-place edit was intended, so it's worth knowing if you need `edit` later.
